{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"object-static-methods","title":"Object Static Methods","group":"Arrays & Objects","order":27,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">The <code>Object</code> constructor carries the toolbox for inspecting, copying, converting and grouping objects.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Object.keys / values / entries(o)</code></td><td>Own enumerable string keys / values / <code>[key, value]</code> pairs</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.fromEntries(iterable)</code></td><td>Pairs → object (inverse of <code>entries</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.assign(target, ...src)</code></td><td>Copy own enumerable props into <code>target</code> (mutates, shallow)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.create(proto, descriptors?)</code></td><td>New object with the given prototype</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.getPrototypeOf / setPrototypeOf</code></td><td>Read / change the prototype</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.defineProperty / defineProperties</code></td><td>Add props with explicit attributes</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.freeze / seal / preventExtensions</code></td><td>Restrict changes</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.hasOwn(o, k)</code></td><td>Own-property check (ES2022)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.is(a, b)</code></td><td>SameValue equality</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.groupBy(items, fn)</code></td><td>Group into a null-prototype object (ES2024)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Object.getOwnPropertyNames / getOwnPropertySymbols</code></td><td>Include non-enumerables / symbols</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-transform\"></i>entries ⇄ fromEntries: transform an object</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const prices = { apple: 1.2, bread: 2.5, milk: 0.99 };\nconst doubled = Object.fromEntries(\n  Object.entries(prices).map(([k, v]) =&gt; [k, v * 2])\n);\nconsole.log(doubled);\nconst cheap = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(prices).filter(([, v]) =&gt; v &lt; 2));\nconsole.log(cheap);\nconsole.log(Object.fromEntries(new Map([[\"x\", 1]])));\nconsole.log(Object.fromEntries(new URLSearchParams(\"q=js&amp;page=2\")));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ apple: 2.4, bread: 5, milk: 1.98 }\n{ apple: 1.2, milk: 0.99 }\n{ x: 1 }\n{ q: 'js', page: '2' }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-copy\"></i>assign vs spread</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const defaults = { theme: \"light\", lang: \"en\" };\nconst user = { lang: \"hi\" };\nconst merged = Object.assign({}, defaults, user);\nconst spread = { ...defaults, ...user };\nconsole.log(merged, spread);\nObject.assign(defaults, { theme: \"dark\" });   // mutates the target\nconsole.log(defaults);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ theme: 'light', lang: 'hi' } { theme: 'light', lang: 'hi' }\n{ theme: 'dark', lang: 'en' }</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Later sources win. <code>Object.assign</code> <em>invokes setters</em> on the target; spread defines fresh properties. Both are shallow copies.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-category\"></i>Object.groupBy (ES2024)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const inventory = [\n  { name: \"asparagus\", type: \"veg\", qty: 5 },\n  { name: \"banana\", type: \"fruit\", qty: 0 },\n  { name: \"goat\", type: \"meat\", qty: 23 },\n  { name: \"cherry\", type: \"fruit\", qty: 5 },\n];\nconst byType = Object.groupBy(inventory, ({ type }) =&gt; type);\nconsole.log(Object.keys(byType), byType.fruit.length);\nconst stock = Map.groupBy(inventory, ({ qty }) =&gt; (qty &gt; 0 ? \"ok\" : \"restock\"));\nconsole.log(stock.get(\"restock\"));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 'veg', 'fruit', 'meat' ] 2\n[ { name: 'banana', type: 'fruit', qty: 0 } ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-sparkles\"></i>Object.create</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const animal = { speak() { return `${this.name} makes a sound`; } };\nconst dog = Object.create(animal);\ndog.name = \"Rex\";\nconsole.log(dog.speak(), Object.getPrototypeOf(dog) === animal);\nconst dict = Object.create(null);          // no prototype at all\ndict.key = \"v\";\nconsole.log(\"toString\" in dict, dict);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Rex makes a sound true\nfalse [Object: null prototype] { key: 'v' }</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Object.keys vs Object.getOwnPropertyNames vs Reflect.ownKeys?</summary><div><p><code>Object.keys</code> → own <strong>enumerable</strong> string keys. <code>getOwnPropertyNames</code> → own string keys including non-enumerable. <code>Reflect.ownKeys</code> → all own keys, strings and symbols, enumerable or not.</p></div></details></section>"}